0.2.0  2026-11-24
    - installed mods are told apart: chosen by you (i) or installed as a
      dependency (d); list, show and the full screen mode say which mods
      need each one, and point out dependencies nothing needs
    - search: is:chosen, is:dep, is:needed, is:orphan
    - full screen mode: i / I go through all, installed, chosen,
      dependencies, unneeded dependencies, not installed, updates, marked
    - full screen mode: p puts the description at the bottom, on the
      right (everything about the mod, scrolled with J K) or off;
      remembered in "settings"
    - modlists: save, show, install, pin, sync, delete; w and o in the
      full screen mode
    - keep and auto (and e in the full screen mode) change a mod between
      chosen and dependency
    - fixed: a key typed right after Esc was lost
    - help is paged when the terminal is short; S orders backwards,
      C clears all marks, r says how many it marked
    - tests/modlist.sh, which needs no network
    - an upgrade that is refused (a file belongs to another module or
      is in the way) now leaves the old version installed
    - installing a module by name that came in as a dependency keeps
      it as yours, so autoremove no longer deletes it
    - reinstalling a metapackage no longer registers it twice
    - fixed a one-byte overflow reading long names in the module list
    - a broken line in the installed list no longer mixes up files

0.1.0  2026-11-24
    First release.
    - module list from CKAN-meta, with download counts
    - dependencies: depends, any_of, provides, conflicts, version limits,
      DLC detection; recommended and suggested modules offered
    - install rules: find, find_regexp, file, as, filter, filter_regexp,
      include_only, find_matches_files, install_to GameRoot
    - checks SHA-256 or SHA-1 of every download; tries every mirror
    - remove with dependents and orphans; upgrade; pinned versions;
      autoremove; clean
    - remembered game instances, shared module list
    - full screen mode: colours (habamax), search, five orders,
      detail pane, keyboard only
    - safe against path traversal, symlinks and zip bombs
